cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  String Readability Study — Replication Package: An Empirical
  Investigation to Understand the Impact of String Interpolation
  on Program Readability and Comprehension
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: dataset
authors:
  # TODO before release: add co-authors in paper order, and ORCID iDs if available.
  - given-names: Daniel
    family-names: Ogenrwot
    email: ogenrwot@unlv.nevada.edu
    affiliation: University of Nevada, Las Vegas
repository-code: https://github.com/unlv-evol/string-readability-study
abstract: >-
  Replication package for a mixed-method study of how string
  interpolation and string concatenation affect program
  readability, comprehension, and debugging efficiency. Includes
  the web-based experiment platform, raw and processed response
  data from 314 participants across 16 programming tasks, the
  qualitative codebooks and LLM prompts used for thematic
  analysis, and the analysis scripts and figures reported in the
  paper.
keywords:
  - program comprehension
  - program readability
  - string interpolation
  - string concatenation
  - empirical software engineering
  - human study
license: MIT
